"bm_george|Ari rolled his right ankle and stretched a ligament. That is a mild sprain.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Most mild sprains heal in about 2 weeks. A brace or a walking boot protects the ankle while it heals.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|If he plays on Saturday in a brace, about 1 in 10 kids roll it again. With only tape, about 2 in 10.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Because Ari hides pain, I updated: if he plays on Saturday, about 3 in 10 roll it again in a brace, and about 5 in 10 with tape.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|A second sprain takes about 6 weeks to heal. That\u2019s three times as long.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|My forecast assumes Ari stops playing when it hurts. Most kids do, but not all.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
"bm_george|Ari\u2019s grandma says he hides pain, so the pain check may not work for him.":"data:audio/ogg;base64,",
